{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":1383548,"num_turns":78,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5e1ec32c-4097-4939-8cb3-1a1311323d70","total_cost_usd":9.227272999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":1995,"cache_creation_input_tokens":185467,"cache_read_input_tokens":9821636,"output_tokens":97922,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":185467,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1579,"cache_read_input_tokens":202509,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2341,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2341},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3675,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00376,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":1995,"outputTokens":97922,"cacheReadInputTokens":9821636,"cacheCreationInputTokens":185467,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":9.223512999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Implementation and correctness gates are done; the before/after `cmd/curator` measurement is running and will notify me.\n\n**Where things stand:**\n\nThe tester's regression was real, and I fixed it by deleting the mechanism that caused it rather than guarding it. The withdrawn candidate cached ancestor `*os.Root` handles across the **digest** phase, so a directory renamed out of GOROOT and replaced kept feeding detached bytes into the hash while `os.SameFile` compared against the original inode and passed.\n\nWhat I changed in `internal/godriver/fingerprint.go`:\n\n- **Digest phase restored to the accepted code**, character for character — `root.Open(record.path)` per file, then `Stat`/`SameFile`/size guards/`copyWithContext`. `scopedDirs` is gone. Path binding isn't *revalidated*; it's the same resolution the accepted implementation performs, so there is nothing left to diverge.\n- **Collection phase keeps the scoped descent only for the per-entry `Lstat` of files and links** — the one step whose result something else re-anchors (files by the digest-phase open + `SameFile`, links by root-anchored `Readlink`/`Stat`). Directory records, which nothing revisits, now take a **full-path** `Lstat`, and every directory is listed through a handle opened by its full path.\n\nThat is the guarantee the rework directive asked for, by a cheaper route: resolving the cached directory from GOROOT before each reuse costs the same syscalls as just opening the file by full path, adds an identity check a rename-and-back would still pass, and leaves new code on the trust boundary.\n\n**Measured so far** (real exit codes, standalone commands):\n\n- Fingerprint A/B, same process, host GOROOT (16093 records): legacy 1.56–1.59 s/op → **1.163–1.168 s/op, 1.35x**. Deliberately below the withdrawn candidate's 3.4x — that difference *is* the price of the path binding.\n- `go test ./internal/godriver` exit 0 (30.1s); same with `CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT` exit 0 (34.9s); go-v1 vector run exit 0 including `TestFingerprintImplementationMatchesRC4ToolchainVector`; build, vet, gofmt, `git diff --check` all exit 0.\n- `fingerprint.go` coverage: collect 100%, digest 85.4%, descend 88.7%.\n- `golangci-lint` **not run** — absent from this host, and installation is forbidden by the task.\n\nThe tester's `TestScopedDirsDoesNotReadFromAReplacedDirectory` couldn't be kept verbatim because the helper it tested is the defect. Its property was promoted to `TestFingerprintDigestPhaseResolvesEveryFileFromTheRoot`, which applies the same rename-and-replace at the real phase boundary of the real `fingerprintToolchain` and requires matching **code and detail**, plus ancestor-replacement, ABA, symlink-swap and deterministic boundary-cancellation cases. I'll flag that promotion explicitly for review.\n\nOne correction to the prior artifact: `os.Root` does **not** apply `O_NOFOLLOW` per component — it rejects only links that escape the root. The comments repeating that claim are gone, and the behaviour is now pinned by a test instead of avoided.\n\nStill outstanding: the three timed `cmd/curator` runs (before at 30m, after at 30m, after at default timeout), then re-running the focused tests with the newly added cases, refreshing the attached diff, and the board handoff.","ttft_ms":1834,"ttft_stream_ms":1323,"time_to_request_ms":28,"type":"result","duration_ms":1532831,"uuid":"27934ffa-8593-4613-a086-19bd918ef9d2"}
